  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>A simple pendulum consists of a point mass attached to an inextensible string and suspended from a support.</p><p>The formula to calculate the time period&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>T</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;of a simple pendulum is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math>&nbsp;is the length of the pendulum and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi></math>&nbsp;is the acceleration due to gravity.</p><p>Simplify equation (1) to obtain the relation between the time period and the length.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnspacing=\"0px\" columnalign=\"right center left\"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>T</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">4</mn><msup><mi>&#960;</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>g</mi></mfrac><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#215;</mo><mi>&#120001;</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8733;</mo></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>Equation (2) suggests that the graph between the square of the time period versus the length of the pendulum is a straight line passing through the origin.</p>"
